ptance/**` in the same worktree: never open, stage, modify or delete anything under those paths. Stage with explicit paths only; never `git add -A`.\n\n## Instructions\n- Implement spec.md completely, security first, per its milestones; commit per milestone, local only (never push). End each commit message with:\n  Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <[REDACTED:email]>\n- Keep every step 1-2 control intact. Never weaken security to make something pass. Don't modify src/freight_recovery/, webapp/, root docker-compose.yml, ci.yml.\n- Installs `--ignore-scripts`; exact pins; re-verify against registry/peers; record deviations in mailbox.md.\n- Docker is broken locally. Use the portable PostgreSQL 16 binaries at C:[REDACTED:high_entropy] (your own data dir, port 55433) and a checksum-verified portable MinIO (download into that scratchpad, never into the repo) as the spec describes; portable terraform is at scratchpad/tf/terraform.exe. Stop all servers when done.\n- Run every spec C-section validation script that doesn't need acceptance tests; all must exit 0. Unit + integration tests for the logic you add, including Python parity scripts.\n- Write implementation.md in the run dir (built items, file map, pins, deviations, commands/results, known gaps, final SHA). Append BUILD_COMPLETE or BLOCK to mailbox.md.\n\n## Brain Knowledge\nBrain connected; no relevant entries.\n\nReturn: status, commit list, deviations, command results.","s":true},"resp":{"t":"","s":false},"last_ts":"2026-10-09T01:47:05.928Z","tainted":true,"fb":null,"tools":530}],"handback":{"t":"## Status: BUILD_COMPLETE (fix round 2)\n\nF-01, F-03 and F-04 are fixed in one local commit, **`e3d7ee7ec0f2f313af5a6e2653371640c976f82b`**, on top of the scriber's 8fb6132 on `feat/import-export` (not pushed). The full validation set exits 0, and integration also passes on Node 22.15.0 (the new floor) and 22.23.3. `test:acceptance` was not run because those suites are the tester's; nothing under `*/test-acceptance/**` was touched. `implementation.md` has a \"Fix round 2\" section and `mailbox.md` has the BUILD_COMPLETE entry. Postgres and MinIO are stopped (the MinIO task's \"failed\" exit is my kill).\n\n## F-01: sandbox network guard bypass\n- **Fix (`api/src/imports/sandbox/guard.ts`):** the guard now opens the stdio streams first, then permanently replaces the methods that open connections with the blocking stub:\n  - `connect` on the socket class behind stdin/stdout/stderr (TLS sockets inherit it);\n  - `connect`, `connect6`, `bind`, `bind6`, `listen` and `open` on the native pipe/terminal handle classes behind them.\n  \n  The worker's own stdin/stdout protocol is unaffected because those streams are already open. `process.binding`, `_linkedBinding` and `dlopen` stay blocked.\n- **Tests:** the hostile-worker fixture gained 7 escape routes:\n  - stdin and stdout constructor + `connect`;\n  - calling the prototype's `connect` directly;\n  - the constructor of an active handle;\n  - native handle `open` and `connect`;\n  - deleting and restoring `connect`.\n  \n  `sandbox.int` asserts every one is denied and that 0 connections reach a local listener. Run against the previous guard, the same fixture let 4 TCP connections through and the native `connect` crashed the worker, so the test does catch the bypass.\n- **Docs:** T19 and residual risk 1 in `technical/web-platform-security.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`/`.no.md` and `infra/README.md` now say the guard is best effort and not a security boundary. The real control is the no-egress (no-NAT) task network, and a dedicated no-egress parser task is a launch gate. The READMEs made no such claim, so only their engine notes changed (F-03).\n\n## F-03: Node version floor\n- **Version:** the official Node docs give `module.registerHooks` \"Added in: v23.5.0, v22.15.0\".\n- **Pins:** `engines` (package.json and lock) is now `>=22.15.0 <23 || >=23.5.0 <25`, and `.nvmrc` is 22.23.3.\n- **Docker:** I looked up the image config of the digest-pinned `node:22-alpine` in the registry; it is `NODE_VERSION=22.23.3`, so the api and web Dockerfiles stay as they are. CI picks up `.nvmrc`.\n- **Startup check:** the API now refuses to start in every environment (not only production) when `registerHooks` is missing, with \"Node.js >= 22.15.0 is required (module.registerHooks, used by the parse sandbox guard)\". Every environment, because the worker runs the API's own Node binary and every parse would fail. A config test covers it. README and README.no engine notes are updated.\n\n## F-04: control characters in worker text\n- **One rule (`parse/text.ts`):**\n  - Allowed: tab plus the characters Python's `splitlines` treats as line separators (LF, VT, FF, CR, FS, GS, RS, NEL).\n  - Not allowed: NUL and other C0 controls, DEL, other C1 controls, and lone surrogates.\n- **Worker:** strips them from pdf.js text and from decoded TXT/CSV; a strip is reported as `DECODE_REPLACEMENTS` (registered divergence D4).\n- **Parent (`protocol.ts`):** rejects worker text that still contains any (`parse_failed`). All other worker strings were already re-validated.\n- **Tests:** added in `sandbox.test` and `parse.test`.\n- My first, stricter version also removed FS. That broke the parity case `separators.txt`, so line separators are allowed; parity is back to zero differences. Uploads containing those control bytes were already refused before storage as `binary_content`.\n\n## Command results (HEAD e3d7ee7; portable PG 16.15 :55433, MinIO with SSE-KMS :59000, Python)\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `verify:no-install-scripts`, `prisma:generate`, `typecheck`, `lint` | exit 0 |\n| `npm test` | exit 0 (shared 113, api 287, web 46) |\n| `db:migrate:deploy`, `db:seed`, `db:seed -- --reset`, `ensure-bucket` | exit 0 |\n| `build` | exit 0, `check-dist: OK (36 files)` |\n| `test:integration` | exit 0, 55 passed, 2 placeholder skips; includes the sandbox escape tests and parity on Python 3.14.7 |\n| `audit`, `npm audit signatures` | exit 0 |\n| Parity on Python 3.12.15 | pass |\n| `terraform fmt -check`, `init -backend=false`, `validate` | exit 0 |\n| Full integration on Node 22.15.0 | 55 passed (official portable build; SHA-256 `06067d4f…e27c` matches nodejs.org SHASUMS256) |\n| Full integration on Node 22.23.3 | 55 passed |\n| `test:acceptance` | not run (tester-owned) |\n\nF-02 and F-05 to F-14 were not routed to the builder in this round, so they are unchanged.","s":false},"signals":{"tool_error":15},"tainted_tools":11,"n_tool_calls":541,"scrub_hits":{"high_entropy":3,"email":1}}